text:
Matt H: Quick question — for the JS SDK decision: undici vs relying on global fetch. We need to support ESM/CJS, Node 18+/20, edge runtimes (Vercel, Cloudflare), and keep auth/retry semantics consistent. Thoughts?

Ana P: I'm leaning toward a runtime-detect approach: use global fetch if available, otherwise dynamically import undici for Node. Keeps edge builds small.

Li Z: +1. But watch bundlers and tree-shaking. `import('undici')` in ESM is fine; avoid requiring it in edge builds (Cloudflare/Vercel/Bun). Also call out Bun's global fetch differences.

Samir K: For retries we shouldn't rely on fetch-level retries. Implement retry at SDK layer so we can retry auth-refreshable requests and respect idempotency. E.g. do token refresh then retry once.

Kevin L: Typings are a mess if we import undici types. Suggest typing our fetch as `(input: RequestInfo, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response)` and reference lib.dom. Give users a helper overload to pass their fetch.

Jen R: Can we provide two quick samples (ESM/CJS) in docs and a tiny polyfill snippet for older Node?

Ana P: Yes. Sample approach:

```js
// ESM runtime-detect
const fetchImpl = globalThis.fetch ?? (await import('undici')).fetch;
export function request(url, opts) {
  return fetchImpl(url, {...opts, headers: { ... }});
}
```

Matt H: What about auth - how to inject Authorization header and retries? Also how to avoid double-adding headers when user supplies their own fetch that attaches auth?

Samir K: SDK should NOT mutate user fetch's behavior. Wrap the user fetch: create a small wrapper that injects headers unless present. Pseudocode:

```js
async function wrapper(input, init={}) {
  const headers = new Headers(init.headers || {});
  if (!headers.has('authorization')) {
    headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
  }
  let res = await fetchImpl(input, {...init, headers});
  if (res.status === 401) {
     await refreshToken();
     headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
     res = await fetchImpl(input, {...init, headers});
  }
  return res;
}
```

Kevin L: For types show a helper signature:

```ts
type FetchLike = (input: RequestInfo, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>
export function createClient(opts: { fetch?: FetchLike }) { ... }
```

Li Z: Edge runtimes: recommend users pass in fetch for deno/cloudflare; for Node we auto-detect. Document build-time bundler caveats (esbuild: add `--conditions=node`? or explicit externals).

Jen R: For polyfills: small snippet:

```js
// Node <18
import fetch from 'undici';
globalThis.fetch = fetch;
```

Ana P: Also note removing global polyfills in user's environment can break other libs — better to instruct users to pass fetch into client.

DevEx Bot: Added a docs task: https://redwood.atlassian.net/browse/DEVEX-123 :thumbsup:

Matt H: Cool. Action items: Ana to draft docs + samples, Samir to write retry/auth wrapper, Kevin to add typings PR. I'll open PR with runtime-detect pattern.

Ana P: I'll draft and include ESM/CJS snippets and a small paragraph on "why we choose runtime-detect + opt-in undici" and guidance for Private deployments + VPC.

Samir K: I'll also add a small test matrix (Node 16/18/20, Cloudflare, Vercel Edge, Bun) — will include in PR.

Matt H: thanks all :rocket:
